From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: sunxi: sun55i-pck600: add A733 (sun60iw2) support

The A733 (sun60iw2) carries the same PCK-600 power controller as the A523:
per-domain 0x1000 register windows, PWPR@0x0 / PWSR@0x8, power mode 0x8 = on.
Confirmed on silicon (the 8 GiB board): the USB2 domain status at 0x07060000 + 8*0x1000 +
0x8 = 0x07068008 reads 0x8 (boot-on), matching the stride, offset and mode
encoding the A523 driver already uses. The A733 domain map has 11 entries
(index 0..10); PD_USB2 = 8. Adds the dt-bindings header and a binding schema
covering both compatibles.

The A733 support is deliberately attach-only (keep_boot_state): every domain is
registered GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON and the delay/sequence registers are left
untouched. Rationale:

  - The immediate consumer is dwc3/USB2, whose domain is boot-on and must stay
    on. Registering the provider is what lets that consumer attach instead of
    deferring forever; no gating is wanted.
  - The A523's per-domain power-sequencing delays (device_ctrl0/1, logic power
    switch, off2on) are NOT silicon-verified for the A733. Programming them and
    letting genpd gate the ten unused domains would be speculative writes with
    an unverified handshake. Holding boot state is the correct minimal, safe
    behaviour until the sequence is proven on hardware.

Reset and clock are made optional: the A733 leaves the PPU block clocked and
out of reset by boot firmware and wires neither in DT. The A523 wires both and
its DT still requires them (enforced by the binding). The optional variants
acquire them unchanged when present, so this is not an A523 behaviour change.

Domain map cross-checked against allwinner,sun60i-a733-pck-600.h from
Yuanshen Cao's A733 PCK600 series (below) and against the memory map of the
A733 user manual (PPU @0x07060000, and 07060000-0706afff as read on the
board); the USB2 index and the register layout are the silicon-verified
anchor.

Credit: the dt-bindings header in this patch reproduces the include guard,
domain names and indices of the header by Yuanshen Cao
<alex.caoys@gmail.com> from that series, with a comment added; the
compatible string and the domain names match his driver change. Both are in
mainline as f287826fd7e4 ("dt-bindings: power: Add Support for Allwinner
A733 PCK600 Power Domain Controller") and a46e905cd14a ("pmdomain: sunxi:
Add support for A733 to Allwinner PCK600 driver"). This patch differs from
his driver change: it keeps the boot state instead of programming the delay
registers, and it makes the clock optional as well as the reset. The
binding schema file is written for this series; mainline documents both
compatibles in allwinner,sun20i-d1-ppu.yaml instead.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260305-b4-pck600-a733-v2-0-ba6bbed7d253@gmail.com
Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
@@ -52,6 +52,15 @@
 	u32 logic_power_switch0_delay;
 	u32 logic_power_switch1_delay;
 	u32 off2on_delay;
+	/*
+	 * Attach-only mode. When set, every domain is registered
+	 * GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON and the delay/sequence registers are left
+	 * untouched: the driver only lets consumers attach and holds the
+	 * boot-time power state, it never gates a domain. Used by the A733,
+	 * whose per-domain power-sequencing delays are not silicon-verified;
+	 * its USB2 domain is boot-on and must simply stay on.
+	 */
+	bool keep_boot_state;
 };
 
 struct sunxi_pck600_pd {
@@ -151,11 +160,17 @@
 	if (IS_ERR(base))
 		return PTR_ERR(base);
 
-	rst = devm_reset_control_get_exclusive_released(dev, NULL);
+	/*
+	 * Reset and clock are optional: the A733 leaves the PPU block clocked
+	 * and out of reset by boot firmware (its USB2 domain is boot-on) and
+	 * wires neither in DT. On the A523 both are present and are acquired
+	 * exactly as before.
+	 */
+	rst = devm_reset_control_get_optional_exclusive_released(dev, NULL);
 	if (IS_ERR(rst))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(rst), "failed to get reset control\n");
 
-	clk = devm_clk_get_enabled(dev, NULL);
+	clk = devm_clk_get_optional_enabled(dev, NULL);
 	if (IS_ERR(clk))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(clk), "failed to get clock\n");
 
@@ -167,7 +182,12 @@
 		pd->genpd.power_on = sunxi_pck600_power_on;
 		pd->base = base + PPU_REG_SIZE * i;
 
-		sunxi_pck600_pd_setup(pd, desc);
+		if (desc->keep_boot_state)
+			pd->genpd.flags = GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON;
+		else
+			sunxi_pck600_pd_setup(pd, desc);
+
+		/* "false" => domain starts powered (its boot state). */
 		ret = pm_genpd_init(&pd->genpd, NULL, false);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "failed to initialize power domain\n");
@@ -209,11 +229,34 @@
 	.off2on_delay = 0x8
 };
 
+/*
+ * A733 (sun60iw2) PCK-600. Same register layout as the A523 (per-domain
+ * 0x1000 stride, PWPR@0x0 / PWSR@0x8, PPU_POWER_MODE_ON = 0x8) — the USB2
+ * domain status at 0x07060000 + 8 * 0x1000 + 0x8 = 0x07068008 reads 0x8
+ * (boot-on) on silicon, confirming stride, offset and mode encoding. The
+ * domain map has 11 entries (index 0..10); PD_USB2 = 8. keep_boot_state is
+ * set: only attach + hold boot state, no unverified gating (see the desc).
+ */
+static const char * const sun60i_a733_pck600_pd_names[] = {
+	"VI", "DE_SYS", "VE_DEC", "VE_ENC", "NPU", "GPU_TOP",
+	"GPU_CORE", "PCIE", "USB2", "VO", "VO1"
+};
+
+static const struct sunxi_pck600_desc sun60i_a733_pck600_desc = {
+	.pd_names = sun60i_a733_pck600_pd_names,
+	.num_domains = ARRAY_SIZE(sun60i_a733_pck600_pd_names),
+	.keep_boot_state = true,
+};
+
 static const struct of_device_id sunxi_pck600_of_match[] = {
 	{
 		.compatible	= "allwinner,sun55i-a523-pck-600",
 		.data		= &sun55i_a523_pck600_desc,
 	},
+	{
+		.compatible	= "allwinner,sun60i-a733-pck-600",
+		.data		= &sun60i_a733_pck600_desc,
+	},
 	{}
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, sunxi_pck600_of_match);
diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/Kconfig b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/Kconfig
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 	  optional for the H6.
 
 config SUN55I_PCK600
-	tristate "Allwinner A523 PCK-600 power domain driver"
+	tristate "Allwinner A523/A733 PCK-600 power domain driver"
 	depends on ARCH_SUNXI || COMPILE_TEST
 	depends on PM
 	default ARCH_SUNXI
@@ -30,4 +30,4 @@
 	help
 	  Say y to enable the PCK-600 power domain driver. This is required
 	  to enable power to certain peripherals, such as the display and
-	  video engines.
+	  video engines on the A523, and the USB2 domain on the A733.
diff --git a/include/dt-bindings/power/allwinner,sun60i-a733-pck-600.h b/include/dt-bindings/power/allwinner,sun60i-a733-pck-600.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/dt-bindings/power/allwinner,sun60i-a733-pck-600.h
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause) */
+/*
+ * Power-domain indices for the Allwinner A733 (sun60iw2) PCK-600.
+ *
+ * The index of a domain is its position in the PCK-600 register file
+ * (domain N lives at base + N * 0x1000). PD_USB2 = 8 is confirmed on
+ * silicon: its status register at 0x07060000 + 8 * 0x1000 + 0x8 =
+ * 0x07068008 reads 0x8 (boot-on). The other indices follow the A733
+ * hardware domain map.
+ */
+
+#ifndef _DT_BINDINGS_POWER_SUN60I_A733_PCK600_H_
+#define _DT_BINDINGS_POWER_SUN60I_A733_PCK600_H_
+
+#define PD_VI			0
+#define PD_DE_SYS		1
+#define PD_VE_DEC		2
+#define PD_VE_ENC		3
+#define PD_NPU			4
+#define PD_GPU_TOP		5
+#define PD_GPU_CORE		6
+#define PD_PCIE			7
+#define PD_USB2			8
+#define PD_VO			9
+#define PD_VO1			10
+
+#endif /* _DT_BINDINGS_POWER_SUN60I_A733_PCK600_H_ */
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/allwinner,sun55i-a523-pck-600.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/allwinner,sun55i-a523-pck-600.yaml
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/allwinner,sun55i-a523-pck-600.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/power/allwinner,sun55i-a523-pck-600.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Allwinner PCK-600 Power Domain Controller
+
+maintainers:
+  - DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
+
+description:
+  The Allwinner PCK-600 is a power domain controller likely based on the
+  Arm CoreLink PCK-600 Power Control Kit (Power Policy Unit / Q-Channel).
+  It exposes one power domain per Power Policy Unit; each unit occupies a
+  0x1000 register window at "base + index * 0x1000".
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    enum:
+      - allwinner,sun55i-a523-pck-600
+      - allwinner,sun60i-a733-pck-600
+
+  reg:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  clocks:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  resets:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  "#power-domain-cells":
+    const: 1
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+  - "#power-domain-cells"
+
+allOf:
+  # The A523 wires the PPU bus clock and reset in DT and requires both. The
+  # A733 leaves the block clocked and out of reset by boot firmware (its USB2
+  # domain is boot-on) and wires neither.
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          contains:
+            const: allwinner,sun55i-a523-pck-600
+    then:
+      required:
+        - clocks
+        - resets
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    #include <dt-bindings/power/allwinner,sun55i-a523-pck-600.h>
+
+    power-controller@7060000 {
+        compatible = "allwinner,sun55i-a523-pck-600";
+        reg = <0x07060000 0x9000>;
+        clocks = <&r_ccu 19>;
+        resets = <&r_ccu 4>;
+        #power-domain-cells = <1>;
+    };
+
+  - |
+    power-controller@7060000 {
+        compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-pck-600";
+        reg = <0x07060000 0xb000>;
+        #power-domain-cells = <1>;
+    };
+...
